    "faq_a1": "One teacher leads a group, so the cost of each class is shared. Between classes you get instant feedback on your practice, and your teacher grades your homework.",
    "faq_a2": "Yes. Your teacher guides the conversation, gives everyone time to speak and corrects you live, in groups of about 6 to 35 depending on your tier.",
    "faq_a3": "Each class meets on fixed days at a fixed time every week, with the same teacher and group, so choose a class whose schedule fits you. Between classes you can practise whenever you want.",
    "faq_a4": "Every teacher applies with a CV, credentials and a 2-minute video, then leads a 30-minute practice session with a small group of active students before teaching.",
    "faq_a5": "Live classes with your teacher and group on your plan’s schedule, session notes, graded homework, and a practice library with instant feedback, flashcards and exam-format practice.",
    "faq_a6": "Sign up at alimun.com/signup, take the short placement test and choose your tier. Classes are open in English and German; for other languages, join the free waitlist and we email you when it opens.",
    "faq_q1": "How can your classes be so affordable compared to private tutors?",
    "faq_q2": "Does a group class really improve my speaking fluency?",
